ASCII: reproduce ZenGin's nine-digit halfway rounding.

ZenGin's MSVC formatter rounded an exact nine-significant-digit halfway case
away from zero. The current UCRT `%g` follows ties-to-even, turning
`-3055.890625` into `-3055.89062` rather than ZenGin's `-3055.89063` (and
likewise for positive values).

Use one formatter for scalar, vec3 and raw-float writers. It keeps the normal
nine-significant-digit `to_chars` form and three-digit exponent, while exact
halfway values are rendered from their integer decimal significand with the
legacy away-from-zero rule. Newly rendered values retain `%g`'s fixed/scientific
thresholds and trimmed zeroes.

diff --git a/src/archive/ArchiveAscii.cc b/src/archive/ArchiveAscii.cc
--- a/src/archive/ArchiveAscii.cc
+++ b/src/archive/ArchiveAscii.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <array>
 #include <charconv>
